/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250522095607+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250522095627+10'00'" name="c2b20989-b55d-4c07-aa62-8b7a5fdc0b5e" page="3" coords="313.001000,229.655000,575.960000,229.655000,313.001000,218.625000,575.960000,218.625000,313.001000,218.600000,575.963000,218.600000,313.001000,207.570000,575.963000,207.570000,313.001000,207.602000,576.000000,207.602000,313.001000,196.572000,576.000000,196.572000,313.001000,196.547000,575.983000,196.547000,313.001000,185.517000,575.983000,185.517000,313.002000,185.549000,576.007000,185.549000,313.002000,174.519000,576.007000,174.519000,313.002000,174.551000,575.965000,174.551000,313.002000,163.521000,575.965000,163.521000,313.002000,163.496000,575.956000,163.496000,313.002000,152.466000,575.956000,152.466000,313.002000,152.498000,576.010000,152.498000,313.002000,141.468000,576.010000,141.468000,313.002000,141.500000,575.948000,141.500000,313.002000,130.470000,575.948000,130.470000,313.002000,130.444000,346.060000,130.444000,313.002000,119.414000,346.060000,119.414000" rect="312.657000,119.070000,576.355000,230.000000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>We propose that muscle typology is a key determinant of track&#xD;cycling performance in a group of elite and world-class track&#xD;cyclists. Identifying the muscle typology of your track cyclists&#xD;could aid in the selection of specific events, disciplines, or talent&#xD;transfer opportunities. In addition, given that estimated muscle&#xD;typology was associated with key mechanical characteristics&#xD;underpinning track sprint cycling performance, situational race&#xD;tactics and gear selection could be informed by muscle typology,&#xD;which could be used for performance optimization in senior&#xD;athletes.&#xD;&#xD;The findings from this investigation reinforce the implications of&#xD;estimated muscle typology on maximal, short-duration sprint performance&#xD;in world-class and elite-level track cyclists. We report significant&#xD;positive associations between CAZ score (ie, greater estimated </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>proportion of type II fibers) and P</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>max</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>, relative P</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>max</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>, F</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>opt</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>, and F</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>max </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>and&#xD;a significant negative association with absolute fatigue rate when&#xD;partial correlation analysis was used to account for sex. The findings&#xD;derived from this investigation substantiate prior evidence in single&#xD;muscle fibers, highlighting the implications of different mechanical&#xD;and metabolic characteristics of type I and II fibers. We propose that&#xD;these findings provide support for the importance of muscle typology&#xD;in track cycling.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="3" rect="612.000000,137.655000,796.000000,229.655000"
/></highlight
